default: off
off, f() rejected: syntax error
off, term prints as: '()'(foo)  reads back
after set: on
foo() reads as foo()
same as '()'(foo)
distinct from the atom foo
compound: yes
functor '()'/1
on, plain: foo()  reads back
on, quoted name: 'hello world'()  reads back
on, nested: f(a,close(),b)  reads back
on, non-atom arg: '()'(1)  reads back
on, ordinary compound: foo(bar)  reads back
on, atom: foo  reads back
on, list: [a,b]  reads back
on, curly: {a}  reads back
bare () still rejected: syntax error
